**Definition 3.2 (immutable serving table).** The explicit input $T$ consists of a finite installed set $K_T=Q_T\sqcup H_T$, literal words $a_T:Q_T\to\mathcal W$, all four successors $n_T:Q_T\times\mathcal A\to K_T$, and fixed complete row outputs $o_T:H_T\to\mathcal R_C$. Two distinct installed entries $e_0,e_1$ are fixed with their original labels and faithful inverse labeling. A Read makes one native call at its one literal and then takes the successor for its actual reply. A Halt issues its fixed entire row with no call. The current state is all mutable source-dependent memory. There is no external output decoder or free control transition.

Every installed state counts, including unused Reads, unused Halts and different Halts with equal outputs. Duplicate words, shared states, convergence, cycles and early Halts are allowed. The input gives every record, including words used only from a wrong or divergent entry. Nothing in this volume changes $T$, $e_0,e_1$, any serving literal, any of its four successors, its partition, outputs, duplicates, unused states or cycles.

